{"name":"Aged to Perfection","hex":"#a58ea9","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aged","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Old.","Having the age of."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Old people, collectively."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aged"},{"term":"perfection","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The quality or state of being perfect or complete, so that nothing substandard remains; the highest attainable state or degree of excellence.","A quality, endowment, or acquirement completely excellent; an ideal; faultlessness; especially, the divine attribute of complete excellence."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To perfect."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perfection"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ageing","blocks":[{"text":"Ageing is the process of becoming older. The term refers mainly to humans, many other animals, and fungi; whereas for example, bacteria, perennial plants and some simple animals are potentially biologically immortal. In a broader sense, ageing can refer to single cells within an organism which have ceased dividing, or to the population of a species."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ageing"},{"title":"Perfection","blocks":[{"text":"Perfection is a state, variously, of completeness, flawlessness, or supreme excellence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Disc_Plain_black.svg/330px-Disc_Plain_black.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perfection"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Views_of_a_Foetus_in_the_Womb_detail.jpg/330px-Views_of_a_Foetus_in_the_Womb_detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Views_of_a_Foetus_in_the_Womb_detail.jpg/330px-Views_of_a_Foetus_in_the_Womb_detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedi